        [
          "Schema language",
          "SDL (Schema Definition Language) — the IDL for your API"
        ],
        [
          "T-SQL bridge",
          "SDL is to GraphQL what a database schema is to SQL — defines the type contract. REST is \"stored procedures with URLs\"; GraphQL is \"dynamic SELECT from a typed schema with the client writing the projection.\""
        ],
        [
          "WCF bridge",
          "SDL is GraphQL's WSDL. `[ServiceContract]` + `[OperationContract]` = SDL `type Query`/`type Mutation`. `[DataContract]` types = SDL object types. `Add Service Reference` generated proxy = `graphql-codegen` output. Key difference: WCF is server-driven shape; GraphQL is client-driven projection."
        ]
      ]
    },
